-- ============================================================================
-- Generated by scripts/generate-pcb-reference-migration.js; re-run it and diff instead of editing.
--
-- memory/PCBA states the machines, the stack-up tables and the process variables of bare-board fabrication, but not what the boards
-- consume, some process times and no yield. These were researched and sourced (user decision 2026-11-23: every row carries its
-- source_url, source_date and source_note; ranges are min and max columns, quoted at their midpoint with both ends shown). memory's own
-- values win wherever it states one: these rows only fill what it leaves out. The rows the engine reads carry an item_key; the others are
-- kept for review.
--
-- Staged whole as lookup tables of source version 2026-PCB (beside migration 823's stack-up tables):
--   consumables    104 rows (45 keyed)  memory/PCBA/consumables.csv: consumables and tooling: prepreg, solder mask, dry film, plating metals and their densities, drill and router bits and their life, entry and backup boards, test fixtures, the stamping die
--   process_times   89 rows (16 keyed)  memory/PCBA/process_times.csv: process times and thicknesses: etch-resist tin, ENIG nickel and gold, HASL dwell, the dryer's heated length, the working panel, the solder mask solids
--   yield           28 rows (11 keyed)  memory/PCBA/yield.csv: first-pass fabrication yield by layer count
--
-- Idempotent: a table already staged is left as it is (a changed file ships as a new migration).
-- Verify: SELECT key, value FROM machining_reference_data WHERE source_version = '2026-PCB' AND category = 'lookup_table' ORDER BY 1;
-- ============================================================================

